  "question": {
    "text": "How many of these metals can displace <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> easily from acids. <br/>Fe, Mg, Al, Cu, Ag, Au, Zn",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Fe, Mg, Al and Zn can easily displace <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> from acids due to more reactivity as they are having more <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msubsup></math> than hydrogen. <br/>Cu, Ag, Au can not do it as they have low <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msubsup></math> than hydrogen.",
